Cell[TextData[{
 "For purely string-driven index notation (the einsum DSL), see ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  ButtonBox["EinsteinSummation",
   BaseStyle->"Link",
   ButtonData->"paclet:Wolfram/TensorNetworks/ref/EinsteinSummation"]], 
  "InlineFormula",ExpressionUUID->"07241f2a-9864-4d61-bee2-01ada9adaa8e"],
 " and ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  ButtonBox["IndexedMultiply",
   BaseStyle->"Link",
   ButtonData->"paclet:Wolfram/TensorNetworks/ref/IndexedMultiply"]], 
  "InlineFormula",ExpressionUUID->"55b5251a-ebb9-4215-8385-3deafb3acb23"],
 "; the former produces an ",
 StyleBox["Inactive[TensorContract][\[Ellipsis]]", "Code"],
 " expression that section 2.3 ingests directly."
}], "Text",ExpressionUUID->"05ef4191-ff25-4795-900c-a4ecbdc68d1c"]
}, Open  ]]
}, Open  ]],

Cell[CellGroupData[{

Cell["3. Named topologies", "Section",ExpressionUUID->"8a1ff0f6-bbb1-489f-a182-bbb508905826"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "Most networks used in physics and machine learning have stylized topologies \
\[LongDash] chains, trees, grids, or hierarchical layers \[LongDash] for \
which the paclet ships dedicated random constructors. The driver is ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  ButtonBox["RandomTensorNetwork",
   BaseStyle->"Link",
   ButtonData->"paclet:Wolfram/TensorNetworks/ref/RandomTensorNetwork"]], 
  "InlineFormula",ExpressionUUID->"7f1112ee-534f-4bf0-8eaa-561e1ac0162f"],
 ". Each family is specified as a head bearing the topology name with \
parameters in positional form: ",
 StyleBox["\"MPS\"[L, D, d]", "Code"],
 " for an open matrix product state of length ",
 StyleBox["L", "Code"],
 ", bond dimension ",
 StyleBox["D", "Code"],
 ", and physical (site) dimension ",
 StyleBox["d", "Code"],
 ". Family-specific options follow as standard ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  ButtonBox["Rule",
   BaseStyle->"Link",
   ButtonData->"paclet:Wolfram/TensorNetworks/ref/Rule"]], "InlineFormula",
  ExpressionUUID->"89468d37-48d3-4206-8497-83620f26c238"],
 "s. The tensor entries are drawn from a Gaussian distribution by default; \
the ",
 StyleBox["Method", "Code"],
 " option selects real or complex sampling."
}], "Text",ExpressionUUID->"141bdeac-a6f0-4b7f-9824-980c6139bf43"],

Cell[CellGroupData[{

Cell["3.1. Matrix product states", "Subsection",ExpressionUUID->"817a1d77-7f62-4da2-ab08-98d890fb0958"],

Cell[CellGroupData[{

Cell[TextData[{
 "An MPS on four sites with bond dimension 2 and physical dimension 2. The \
two boundary sites have rank 2 (one bond, one physical leg); the two interior \
sites have rank 3 (left bond, right bond, physical). Set ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  ButtonBox["SeedRandom",
   BaseStyle->"Link",
   ButtonData->"paclet:Wolfram/TensorNetworks/ref/SeedRandom"]], 
  "InlineFormula",ExpressionUUID->"0fc43ba6-a2ec-46ac-9743-228b996e912f"],
 " first to make the construction reproducible."
}], "Text",ExpressionUUID->"d3f8dd34-4d94-4c19-b9b4-370ae139e571"],

Cell[BoxData[
 RowBox[{
  RowBox[{"SeedRandom", "[", "42", "]"}], ";"}]], "Input",
 CellLabel->"In[87]:=",ExpressionUUID->"d8844f08-7426-44ff-9651-e55520961c5d"],

