Cell[CellGroupData[{

Cell["5. Hyperedges and binarization", "Section",ExpressionUUID->"0326714b-ee7d-4b8e-8684-a56b11c57d20"],

Cell["\<\
A hyperedge is an index that joins three or more tensors at once. In ordinary \
tensor diagrams every edge connects exactly two tensors, but the underlying \
mathematics \[LongDash] sums over a shared dummy index \[LongDash] is happy \
to admit any arity. Hyperedges express copy and broadcast structure that \
two-end edges cannot draw, and they appear naturally in symmetry-restricted \
networks, in tensor decompositions like CP, and whenever a delta-function \
constraint couples more than two tensors.\
\>", "Text",ExpressionUUID->"f6c46c99-6556-4a42-bbd2-074d0583c9da"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "Hyperedges are perfectly legal as inputs to ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  ButtonBox["TensorNetwork",
   BaseStyle->"Link",
   ButtonData->"paclet:Wolfram/TensorNetworks/ref/TensorNetwork"]], 
  "InlineFormula",ExpressionUUID->"69556005-18f5-4386-b69c-d480fb6c89d8"],
 ", but most contraction-path search algorithms assume pairwise contractions, \
so the paclet provides a transformation step that binarizes a hyperedge \
network into an equivalent network with only two-end edges. The trick is to \
attach a small auxiliary tensor \[LongDash] a Kronecker-delta \"spider\" \
\[LongDash] to each hyperedge: the spider replaces the n-ary constraint with \
one extra vertex wired pairwise to each tensor that previously shared the \
hyperedge. The resulting network has more tensors but pure binary topology."
}], "Text",ExpressionUUID->"1d91eb00-5f98-4440-aebe-94069fef033f"],

Cell[CellGroupData[{

Cell["Build three tensors sharing index 2 \[LongDash] a genuine hyperedge.", \
"Text",ExpressionUUID->"4c198c1c-d78a-46ed-aefc-8d4560025f8b"],

Cell[BoxData[
 RowBox[{
  RowBox[{"T1", "=", 
   RowBox[{"RandomReal", "[", 
    RowBox[{"1", ",", 
     RowBox[{"{", 
      RowBox[{"2", ",", "3"}], "}"}]}], "]"}]}], ";", " ", 
  RowBox[{"T2", "=", 
   RowBox[{"RandomReal", "[", 
    RowBox[{"1", ",", 
     RowBox[{"{", 
      RowBox[{"3", ",", "4"}], "}"}]}], "]"}]}], ";", " ", 
